</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 457)</h2>
<p><b>⌘S saves, session reels are a sane size, and stuck transcripts are one click from another go.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>⌘S works, and overwrites.</b> Save Session now writes straight back to the session's own file; it only asks where to put it the first time. <b>⇧⌘S</b> is Save As. The shortcut had been dead — the menu was gated on a value that can silently go missing, so it could never re-enable itself.</li>
<li><b>Session reels are far smaller.</b> A reel took the first clip's full resolution — a 4K session came out 657 MB for 102 seconds. Reels now fit inside 1920×1080. That's a bound, not a shape: 4:3 stays 4:3 (2880×2160 becomes 1440×1080), full gate keeps its gate. Set export.reelMaxWidth/Height to 0 to export at source size.</li>
<li><b>Retry a transcript from the note itself</b> — a ↻ button appears on any voice note whose transcript never landed.</li>
<li><b>Notes ▸ Transcribe Again now covers the whole session</b>, not just the clip you're sitting on. Notes on the other clips were exactly the ones left stuck.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
